---
import GitHubIcon from './GitHubIcon.astro'
import InstallTabs from './InstallTabs.astro'
import { GITHUB } from '../data/links'
---
<section id="top" class="mx-auto flex max-w-[1200px] flex-col gap-7 px-5 pt-16 pb-10 sm:px-8 sm:pt-22">
  <p class="vd-in m-0 inline-flex items-center gap-2 self-start rounded-full border border-rule bg-surface px-3 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.06em] text-pencil uppercase">
    <span class="vd-pulse size-[7px] rounded-full bg-teal-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    Spec-driven development for AI coding agents
  </p>
  <h1 class="vd-in m-0 max-w-[1000px] text-5xl leading-[0.98] font-semibold tracking-[-0.045em] sm:text-7xl lg:text-[84px]" style="animation-delay: 80ms">
    Every task your agent finishes comes with <span class="vd-mark rounded-lg px-3">proof</span>.
  </h1>
  <div class="vd-in flex flex-wrap items-start gap-12" style="animation-delay: 160ms">
    <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-[1_1_420px] flex-col gap-5">
      <p class="m-0 max-w-[560px] text-lg leading-relaxed text-body sm:text-xl">
        VibeDoc keeps your plan, specs and memory as markdown in your repo. Claude Code, Cursor or any MCP agent works them
        task by task, and you review each one on its tests, screenshots and video.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="#demo" class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-violet px-5 text-[15px] font-medium text-night no-underline hover:brightness-110">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 4.5v15l13-7.5Z"></path></svg>
          Watch it work
        </a>
        <a href={GITHUB} data-goatcounter-click="github-hero" class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-rule-strong bg-surface px-5 text-[15px] no-underline hover:border-pencil">
          <GitHubIcon />
          Star on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="m-0 text-[13px] text-pencil">Works with Claude Code · Cursor · Windsurf · Codex · any MCP client</p>
    </div>
    <InstallTabs />
  </div>
</section>
